# Date words that alone take a more frequent non-date sense. A preposition,
# demonstrative, number or year beside the word keeps the date sense.
# лютий, лютим: adjective "fierce, cruel, severe" (Wiktionary "лютий", Ukrainian,
# adjective). The month in a date takes a number: "5 лютого", "у лютому".
лютий
лютим
